{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OBSERVATION\nRCA complete. The five listed keys still let an empty env var override a non-empty file value. Scratch config set verify.require_environment='prod-env', verify.opcert_enforce_since='refs/tags/enforce', identity.enforce_since='refs/tags/identity', mcp.auth_required_scopes=['tickets:write','tickets:read'], and mcp.auth_jwt_expected_typ='at+jwt'. With the corresponding env vars present but empty, load_config resolved them as '', '', '', (), and ''.\n\nHYPOTHESIS\nThe mechanism is precedence plus permissive coercion. config._ordered_layers places env after project config; _config_sources.env_overrides treats mere presence of REBAR_<SECTION>_<KEY> as an override even when the value is ''. _config_coercion._as_str returns str(v), so '' survives; _as_str_tuple splits '' and drops empty entries, yielding (). Consumers then interpret the empty result as disabled: verify_opcert uses cfg.verify.require_environment / opcert_enforce_since, verify_authorship uses cfg.identity.enforce_since, mcp_server passes required_scopes=list(... ) or None, and _mcp_auth only enforces expected_typ when the string is truthy.\n\nCONFIRMATION\nThe deterministic subprocess experiment used REBAR_CONFIG pointing at scratch config plus the five empty env vars. Evidence that would disprove the RCA would be ConfigError on empty env, or file values winning over empty env; neither occurred. Working comparison: the earlier boolean fix made _as_bool('') raise, but these string/tuple coercers still accept empty because empty is meaningful for some other keys.\n\nSUGGESTED FIX DIRECTION\nNeeds a small design choice, not a blanket coercer change: add per-key empty-env disposition (meaningful unset vs fault). For the protection-direction keys, fail closed when env is present empty; preserve documented empty defaults and consumer-side fail-closed checks for the already-safe keys."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788737927128029001,"uuid":"aff304da-f734-4957-9291-58624b6b7a26"}